      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could what Tristan mentioned. Though you could also do a quick fix by changing the regex and using `tr`.\n\nSo something like:\n\n```\ngrep -e \u0027^+\\(ZTEST\\|ZTEST_F\\|ZTEST_USER\\|ZTEST_USER_F\\)([^)]+)\u0027 |\n     tr \u0027\\n\u0027 \u0027\u0027 |\n     grep -v test_; then\n```\n\nThe `([^)]+)` should match the first open and closing parens. Then the `tr` command will replace newlines with nothing.",
      "revId": "2d1cf0ded81c52f7e970b4879a22cbad20661208",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
